= Political Violence

A wave of political violence has broken out: threats against election workers and judges, attacks on politicians, and clashes at protests. Experts warn the country is entering a dangerous new phase.

- @violence_condemn: Condemn violence from every side
- @violence_security: Increase security for officials and election workers
- @violence_blame: Blame the other side

@violence_condemn
on-arrival: violence_done = 1; polarization -= 1.5; pro_democracy += 2; farright_strength -= 1; farleft_strength -= 0.5; institutions += 1

A rare moment of cross-party agreement offers hope.

@violence_security
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Need 1 budget.
on-arrival: violence_done = 1; budget -= 1; election_admin += 4; institutions += 1; federal_law_loyalty += 0.02

Protection of the people who run democracy becomes a priority.

@violence_blame
on-arrival: violence_done = 1; polarization += 3; dem_enthusiasm += 0.5; gop_enthusiasm += 0.8; farright_strength += 1.5

Rhetoric worsens, with predictable results.
